// IFL 2016 Paper - Figure 2, 4, 5 & 7
// Lazy Factorial: parameter n is non-strict.
// Demonstrates:
// - Stage 2: lazy tagging of (n - 1)
// - Stage 3: lambda lifting into helper function facl_1
// - Stage 4: explicit thunk creation (thunk (facl_1 n)) and eval(n)
// - Stage 5: dual entry point (facl_lazy vs facl)

start = facl 6

facl n =
  if (n == 0)
    1
    (n * facl (n - 1))
